1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,268
Two candles, exactly the same green. Same open, same close.

2
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:16,970
In one, buyers pushed hard. In the other, sellers simply stepped back.

3
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:20,894
One number shows that difference: delta.

4
00:00:21,894 --> 00:00:26,805
Hello, this is episode thirteen of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:27,255 --> 00:00:32,400
Last time: the footprint chart. Bid x ask at every price.

6
00:00:32,851 --> 00:00:39,696
Today: delta, and its running total, cumulative delta or CVD.

7
00:00:40,696 --> 00:00:46,103
Delta means volume traded at the ask minus volume traded at the bid.

8
00:00:46,553 --> 00:00:50,837
At the ask are those buying with market orders, the buyers in a hurry.

9
00:00:51,287 --> 00:00:58,993
At the bid are those selling with market orders, the sellers in a hurry. Delta shows who was in more of a hurry.

10
00:00:59,993 --> 00:01:02,266
Remember the candle from the last episode.

11
00:01:02,716 --> 00:01:08,827
All the ask volume adds up to 655. All the bid volume to 390.

12
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:17,637
655 minus 390: delta +265. In this candle the buyers in a hurry were ahead.

13
00:01:18,637 --> 00:01:22,190
Positive delta: aggressive buyers were heavier.

14
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:26,610
Negative delta: aggressive sellers were heavier.

15
00:01:27,061 --> 00:01:32,860
And delta near zero: an even fight on both sides. Nobody won.

16
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:37,830
Each candle's delta becomes a bar under the chart.

17
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:44,000
A green bar up means positive. A red bar down means negative.

18
00:01:44,451 --> 00:01:50,878
But a single bar is just one candle's story. For the full picture, you add them up.

19
00:01:51,878 --> 00:01:58,878
CVD, cumulative delta: keep adding each candle's delta to the running total.

20
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:10,091
Deltas of six candles: +265, +120, -80, +150, -40, +200.

21
00:02:10,541 --> 00:02:22,427
Running total: 265, 385, 305, 455, 415, 615. That is the CVD line.

22
00:02:23,427 --> 00:02:26,117
Now put CVD next to price.

23
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:32,993
Price makes a new high and CVD makes a new high too: buyers are really buying.

24
00:02:33,442 --> 00:02:41,254
If they move together, the trend is healthy. If they split, be careful. That is next episode.

25
00:02:42,254 --> 00:02:46,042
Remember: delta and volume are different things.

26
00:02:46,492 --> 00:02:55,399
Candle P: volume 1000, but 510 at the ask and 490 at the bid. Delta only +20.

27
00:02:55,849 --> 00:03:04,287
Candle Q: volume only 400, but 350 at the ask and 50 at the bid. Delta +300.

28
00:03:04,737 --> 00:03:10,536
More volume does not mean more push. Delta shows which way the push went.

29
00:03:11,536 --> 00:03:14,462
CVD is counted from some starting point.

30
00:03:14,912 --> 00:03:20,710
Most tools restart it from zero at the start of each session or day.

31
00:03:21,161 --> 00:03:28,710
Or from a chosen point, like a major high or low. That is called anchored CVD.

32
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:35,196
And the same truth again: spot forex and gold have no real delta.

33
00:03:35,646 --> 00:03:44,893
Delta indicators on MT5 estimate it: an uptick is counted as a buy, a downtick as a sell.

34
00:03:45,343 --> 00:03:54,904
It can be a useful estimate, but it is not real. Real delta comes from futures: gold futures, index futures or a crypto exchange.

35
00:03:55,904 --> 00:03:57,472
So, today's summary.

36
00:03:57,922 --> 00:04:03,642
Delta is ask minus bid: buyers in a hurry minus sellers in a hurry.

37
00:04:04,091 --> 00:04:11,642
CVD is the running total of delta. If price and CVD move together, the trend is healthy.

38
00:04:12,091 --> 00:04:17,656
More volume is not more push. And real delta comes from futures.

39
00:04:18,656 --> 00:04:25,187
Next episode: delta divergence. When price says one thing and delta another.

40
00:04:25,637 --> 00:04:30,548
If this was useful, subscribe and save the playlist.

41
00:04:30,998 --> 00:04:37,189
For trade setups, our Telegram and Instagram are in the description. See you in the next episode.

